H4600.definition:
a primitive root;
to press, i.e. to pierce, emasculate, handle
KJV: bruised, stuck, be pressed.

H4601.definition:
or מַעֲכָת; (Joshua 13:13), from H4600 (מָעַךְ); depression;
Maakah (or Maakath), the name of a place in Syria, also of a Mesopotamian, of three Israelites, and of four Israelitesses and one Syrian woman
KJV: Maachah, Maachathites. See also H1038 (בֵּית מַעֲכָה).

H4602.definition:
patrial from H4601 (מַעֲכָה);
a Maakathite, or inhabitant of Maakah
KJV: Maachathite.

H4603.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cover up; used only figuratively, to act covertly, i.e. treacherously
KJV: transgress, (commit, do a) trespass(-ing).

H4604.definition:
from H4603 (מָעַל);
treachery, i.e. sin
KJV: falsehood, grievously, sore, transgression, trespass, [idiom] very.

H4605.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
properly, the upper part, used only adverbially with prefix upward, above, overhead, from the top, etc.
KJV: above, exceeding(-ly), forward, on ([idiom] very) high, over, up(-on, -ward), very.

H4606.definition:
(Aramaic) from H5954 (עֲלַל);
(only in plural as singular) the setting (of the sun)
KJV: going down.

H4607.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
a raising (of the hands)
KJV: lifting up.

H4608.definition:
from H5927 (עָלָה);
an elevation, i.e. (concretely) acclivity or platform; abstractly (the relation or state) a rise or (figuratively) priority
KJV: ascent, before, chiefest, cliff, that goeth up, going up, hill, mounting up, stairs.

H4609.definition:
feminine of H4608 (מַעֲלֶה);
elevation, i.e. the act (literally, a journey to a higher place, figuratively, a thought arising), or (concretely) the condition (literally, a step or grademark, figuratively, a superiority of station); specifically a climactic progression (in certain Psalms)
KJV: things that come up, (high) degree, deal, go up, stair, step, story.

H4610.definition:
from H4608 (מַעֲלֶה) and (the plural of) H6137 (עַקְרָב);
Steep of Scorpions, a place in the Desert
KJV: Maaleh-accrabim, the ascent (going up) of Akrabbim.

H4611.definition:
from H5953 (עָלַל);
an act (good or bad)
KJV: doing, endeavour, invention, work.

H4612.definition:
from H5975 (עָמַד);
(figuratively) a position
KJV: attendance, office, place, state.

H4613.definition:
from H5975 (עָמַד);
literally a foothold
KJV: standing.

H4615.definition:
from H6009 (עָמַק);
a deep
KJV: deep, depth.

H4616.definition:
from H6030 (עָנָה);
properly, heed, i.e. purpose; used only adverbially, on account of (as a motive or an aim), teleologically, in order that
KJV: because of, to the end (intent) that, for (to,... 's sake), [phrase] lest, that, to.

H4617.definition:
from H6030 (עָנָה);
a reply (favorable or contradictory)
KJV: answer, [idiom] himself.

H4618.definition:
from H6031 (עָנָה), in the sense of depression or tilling;
a furrow
KJV: [phrase] acre, furrow.

H4619.definition:
from H6095 (עָצָה); closure;
Maats, an Israelite
KJV: Maaz.

H4621.definition:
from an unused root meaning to hew;
an axe
KJV: ax, tongs.

H4622.definition:
from H6113 (עָצָר);
objectively, a hindrance
KJV: restraint.

H4623.definition:
from H6113 (עָצָר);
subjectively, control
KJV: rule.

H4624.definition:
from an unused root meaning to repress;
a parapet
KJV: battlement.

H4625.definition:
from H6140 (עָקַשׁ);
a crook (in a road)
KJV: crooked thing.

H4626.definition:
from H6168 (עָרָה);
a nude place, i.e. (literally) the pudenda, or (figuratively) a vacant space
KJV: nakedness, proportion.

H4627.definition:
from H6148 (עָרַב), in the sense of trading;
traffic; by implication, mercantile goods
KJV: market, merchandise.

H4628.definition:
or (feminine) מַעֲרָבָה; from H6150 (עָרַב), in the sense of shading;
the west (as a region of the evening sun)
KJV: west.

H4629.definition:
from H6168 (עָרָה);
a nude place, i.e. a common
KJV: meadows.

H4630.definition:
feminine of H4629 (מַעֲרֶה);
an open spot
KJV: army (from the margin).

H4631.definition:
from H5783 (עוּר);
a cavern (as dark)
KJV: cave, den, hole.

H4632.definition:
the same as H4631 (מְעָרָה); cave;
Mearah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Mearah.

H4633.definition:
from H6186 (עָרַךְ);
an arrangement, i.e. (figuratively) mental disposition
KJV: preparation.

H4634.definition:
feminine of H4633 (מַעֲרָךְ);
an arrangement; concretely, a pile; specifically a military array
KJV: army, fight, be set in order, ordered place, rank, row.

H4635.definition:
from H6186 (עָרַךְ);
an arrangement, i.e. (concretely) a pile (of loaves)
KJV: row, shewbread.

H4636.definition:
from H6191 (עָרַם), in the sense of stripping;
bare
KJV: naked.

H4638.definition:
a form of H4630 (מַעֲרָה); waste;
Maarath, a place in Palestine
KJV: Maarath.

H4639.definition:
from H6213 (עָשָׂה);
an action (good or bad); generally, a transaction; abstractly, activity; by implication, a product (specifically, a poem) or (generally) property
KJV: act, art, [phrase] bakemeat, business, deed, do(-ing), labor, thing made, ware of making, occupation, thing offered, operation, possession, [idiom] well, (handy-, needle-, net-) work(ing, -manship), wrought.

H4640.definition:
from H6213 (עָשָׂה); operative;
Maasai, an Israelite
KJV: Maasiai.

H4641.definition:
or מַעֲשֵׂיָהוּ; from H4639 (מַעֲשֶׂה) and H3050 (יָהּ); work of Jah;
Maasejah, the name of sixteen Israelites
KJV: Maaseiah.

H4642.definition:
from H6231 (עָשַׁק);
oppression
KJV: oppression, [idiom] oppressor.

H4643.definition:
or מַעֲשַׂר; and (in plural) feminine מַעַשְׂרָה; from H6240 (עָשָׂר);
a tenth; especially a tithe
KJV: tenth (part), tithe(-ing).

H4644.definition:
of Egyptian origin;
Moph, the capital of Lower Egypt
KJV: Memphis. Compare H5297 (נֹף).

H4645.definition:
from H6293 (פָּגַע);
an object of attack
KJV: mark.

H4646.definition:
from H5301 (נָפַח);
a breathing out (of life), i.e. expiring
KJV: giving up.

H4647.definition:
from H5301 (נָפַח);
the bellows (i.e. blower) of aforge
KJV: bellows.

H4648.definition:
or מְפִבֹשֶׁת; probably from H6284 (פָּאָה) and H1322 (בֹּשֶׁת); dispeller of shame (i.e. of Baal);
Mephibosheth, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Mephibosheth.

H4649.definition:
a plural apparently from H5130 (נוּף); wavings;
Muppim, an Israelite
KJV: Muppim. Compare H8206 (שֻׁפִּים).

H4650.definition:
from H6327 (פּוּץ);
a breaker, i.e. mallet
KJV: maul.

H4651.definition:
from H5307 (נָפַל);
a falling off, i.e. chaff; also something pendulous, i.e. a flap
KJV: flake, refuse.

H4652.definition:
from H6381 (פָּלָא);
a miracle
KJV: wondrous work.

H4653.definition:
from H6385 (פָּלַג);
a classification
KJV: division.

H4654.definition:
or מַפֵּלָה; from H5307 (נָפַל);
something fallen, i.e. a ruin
KJV: ruin(-ous).

H4655.definition:
from H6403 (פָּלַט);
an escape
KJV: escape.

H4656.definition:
from H6426 (פָּלַץ);
a terror, i.e. an idol
KJV: idol.

H4657.definition:
from an unused root meaning to balance;
a poising
KJV: balancing.

H4658.definition:
from H5307 (נָפַל);
fall, i.e. decadence; concretely, a ruin; specifically a carcase
KJV: carcase, fall, ruin.

H4659.definition:
or (feminine) מִפְעָלָה; from H6466 (פָּעַל);
a performance
KJV: work.

H4660.definition:
from H5310 (נָפַץ);
a smiting to pieces
KJV: slaughter.

H4661.definition:
from H5310 (נָפַץ);
a smiter, i.e. a war club
KJV: battle ax.

H4662.definition:
from H6485 (פָּקַד);
an appointment, i.e. mandate; concretely, a designated spot; specifically, a census
KJV: appointed place, commandment, number.

H4663.definition:
the same as H4662 (מִפְקָד); assignment;
Miphkad, the name of a gate in Jerusalem
KJV: Miphkad.

H4664.definition:
from H6555 (פָּרַץ)lemma פּרַץ missing vowel, corrected to פָּרַץ;
a break (in the shore), i.e. a haven
KJV: breach.

H4665.definition:
from H6561 (פָּרַק);
properly, a fracture, i.e. joint (vertebrae) of the neck
KJV: neck.

H4666.definition:
from H6566 (פָּרַשׂ);
an expansion
KJV: that which...spreadest forth, spreading.

H4667.definition:
from H6585 (פָּשַׂע);
a stride, i.e. (by euphemism) the crotch
KJV: buttocks.

H4668.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
an opener, i.e. a key
KJV: key.

H4669.definition:
from H6605 (פָּתַח);
an aperture, i.e. (figuratively) utterance
KJV: opening.

H4670.definition:
from the same as H6620 (פֶּתֶן);
a stretcher, i.e. a sill
KJV: threshold.

H4671.definition:
or מוֹץ; (Zephaniah 2:2), from H4160 (מוּץ);
chaff (as pressed out, i.e. winnowed or (rather) threshed loose)
KJV: chaff.

H4672.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to come forth to, i.e. appear or exist; transitively, to attain, i.e. find or acquire; figuratively, to occur, meet or be present
KJV: [phrase] be able, befall, being, catch, [idiom] certainly, (cause to) come (on, to, to hand), deliver, be enough (cause to) find(-ing, occasion, out), get (hold upon), [idiom] have (here), be here, hit, be left, light (up-) on, meet (with), [idiom] occasion serve, (be) present, ready, speed, suffice, take hold on.

H4673.definition:
from H5324 (נָצַב);
a fixed spot; figuratively, an office, a military post
KJV: garrison, station, place where...stood.

H4674.definition:
from H5324 (נָצַב);
a station, i.e. military post
KJV: mount.

H4675.definition:
or מִצָּבָה; feminine of H4673 (מַצָּב);
a military guard
KJV: army, garrison.

H4676.definition:
feminine (causatively) participle of H5324 (נָצַב);
something stationed, i.e. a column or (memorial stone); by analogy, an idol
KJV: garrison, (standing) image, pillar.

H4677.definition:
apparently from H4672 (מָצָא) and H3050 (יָהּ); found of Jah;
Metsobajah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Mesobaite.

H4678.definition:
from H5324 (נָצַב);
something stationary, i.e. a monumental stone; also the stock of atree
KJV: pillar, substance.

H4679.definition:
or מְצָד; or (feminine) מְצָדָה; from H6679 (צוּד);
a fastness (as a covert of ambush)
KJV: castle, fort, (strong) hold, munition.

H4680.definition:
a primitive root;
to suck out; by implication, to drain, to squeeze out
KJV: suck, wring (out).

H4681.definition:
active participle feminine of H4680 (מָצָה); drained;
Motsah, a place in Palestine
KJV: Mozah.

H4682.definition:
from H4711 (מָצַץ) in the sense of greedily devouring for sweetness;
properly, sweetness; concretely, sweet (i.e. not soured or bittered with yeast); specifically, an unfermented cake or loaf, or (elliptically) the festival of Passover (because no leaven was then used)
KJV: unleaved (bread, cake), without leaven.

H4683.definition:
from H5327 (נָצָה);
a quarrel
KJV: contention, debate, strife.

H4684.definition:
from H6670 (צָהַל);
a whinnying (through impatience for battle or lust)
KJV: neighing.

H4686.definition:
or (feminine) מְצוּדָה; or מְצֻדָה; for H4685 (מָצוֹד);
a net, or (abstractly) capture; also a fastness
KJV: castle, defense, fort(-ress), (strong) hold, be hunted, net, snare, strong place.

H4687.definition:
from H6680 (צָוָה);
a command, whether human or divine (collectively, the Law)
KJV: (which was) commanded(-ment), law, ordinance, precept.

H4688.definition:
or מְצֹלָה; also מְצוּלָה; or מְצֻלָה; from the same as H6683 (צוּלָה);
a deep place (of water or mud)
KJV: bottom, deep, depth.

H4689.definition:
from H6693 (צוּק);
a narrow place, i.e. (abstractly and figuratively) confinement or disability
KJV: anguish, distress, straitness.

H4690.definition:
or מָצֻק; from H6693 (צוּק);
something narrow, i.e. a column or hilltop
KJV: pillar, situate.

H4691.definition:
or מְצֻקָה; feminine of H4690 (מָצוּק);
narrowness, i.e. (figuratively) trouble
KJV: anguish, distress.

H4692.definition:
or מָצוּר; from H6696 (צוּר);
something hemming in, i.e. (objectively) a mound (of besiegers), (abstractly) a siege, (figuratively) distress; or (subjectively) a fastness
KJV: besieged, bulwark, defence, fenced, fortress, siege, strong (hold), tower.

H4693.definition:
the same as H4692 (מָצוֹר) in the sense of a limit;
Egypt (as the border of Palestine)
KJV: besieged places, defense, fortified.

H4694.definition:
or מְצֻרָה; feminine of H4692 (מָצוֹר);
a hemming in, i.e. (objectively) a mound (of siege), or (subjectively) a rampart (of protection), (abstractly) fortification
KJV: fenced (city, fort, munition, strong hold.

H4695.definition:
from H5327 (נָצָה);
a quarrel
KJV: that contended.

H4696.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be clear, i.e. conspicuous;
the forehead (as open and prominent)
KJV: brow, forehead, [phrase] impudent.

H4697.definition:
from the same as H4696 (מֵצַח);
a shinpiece of armor (as prominent), only plural
KJV: greaves.

H4698.definition:
from H6750 (צָלַל);
a tinkler, i.e. a bell
KJV: bell.
